    "line_start": 73,
    "line_end": 80,
    "literal_excerpt": "    · exact CStarAlgebra.norm_posPart_le _ |>.trans <| imaginaryPart.norm_le a\n    · exact CStarAlgebra.norm_negPart_le _ |>.trans <| realPart.norm_le a\n    · exact CStarAlgebra.norm_negPart_le _ |>.trans <| imaginaryPart.norm_le a\n  · nth_rw 1 [← CStarAlgebra.linear_combination_nonneg a]\n    simp only [Fin.sum_univ_four, Fin.coe_ofNat_eq_mod, Matrix.cons_val, Nat.reduceMod, I_sq,\n      I_pow_three]\n    module\n\n",
    "excerpt_sha256": "1aae2c30ee40e00385a5914a525fb08337ebc3f8946e4654009b7bc2a4074631"
  },
  "existing_pinned_fin_cases_dsimp_only_use": {
    "path": "/workspace/goldbach-formalization/.lake/packages/mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Complex.lean",
    "bytes": 1501,
    "sha256": "f5bed2a7f480fccedc983a42fc26cb46a77d5873a9cbba83ab8ac84c9373595e",
    "line_start": 19,
    "line_end": 25,
    "literal_excerpt": "theorem Algebra.leftMulMatrix_complex (z : ℂ) :\n    Algebra.leftMulMatrix Complex.basisOneI z = !![z.re, -z.im; z.im, z.re] := by\n  ext i j\n  rw [Algebra.leftMulMatrix_eq_repr_mul, Complex.coe_basisOneI_repr, Complex.coe_basisOneI, mul_re,\n    mul_im, Matrix.of_apply]\n  fin_cases j <;> dsimp only [Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one, Matrix.cons_val]\n  · simp only [one_re, mul_one, one_im, mul_zero,\n",
    "excerpt_sha256": "465ea20d0acf754a167cdbb651f5f787550a34224c7f700f270e84fc0c542e42"
  },
  "new_reduction": "Matrix.cons_val is the existing dsimproc for Matrix.vecCons at numeric Fin indices; it selects the same literal row/coordinate. No custom reducer or compiler is introduced.",
